.TH NBL 1 "November 2026" "NBL 0.4.0"
.SH NAME
nbl \- a terminal editor with a project explorer and local code diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nbl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ directory ]
.RI [[ +line[,column] ] " file" ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
NBL is an independent fork of GNU nano 9.3. It adds a right-side project
explorer, configurable themes, and tools for shell, Python, C, and C++.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+W
Write file, close or exit, and search.
.TP
.B F4, F5, F6
Reload the TOML configuration, run the current code, or toggle the terminal.
.TP
.B F7, F8
Toggle the explorer and switch focus.
.TP
.B F9
Copy a buffer selection to the clipboard.
.TP
.B F10, F11, F12
Check the current code with NBL Mentor, jump to the next diagnostic, and
toggle Problems.
.TP
.B Ctrl+]
Complete a token.
.SH EXPLORER
With Explorer focused, press ? for shortcuts. Use g to go to a path,
i to enter a folder, u to go up, and h to go home. Use n and N to create a
file and folder, e to rename, m to move, c to copy, and d to request
deletion. Deleting a directory requires it to be empty.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nbl/config.toml
Theme, editor, explorer, terminal, and executable settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nbl/nblrc
User configuration. Respects XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nbl/
User history and cursor position when enabled. Respects XDG_DATA_HOME.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nano (1),
.BR sh (1),
.BR shellcheck (1)
